  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nWhen encoding a canvas, we should consider the following:\n\nIf the canvas has CanvasToneMapping mode \"extended\", then it should include SMPTE ST 2094-50 metadata that indicates that it uses the extended mode. It should also be converted form its native color space to rec2100-pq.\n\nAlso for canvases that are linear and float16 and are not \"extended\", they should be encoded with the sRGB transfer function (because this will do a better job preserving the lower bits of data, where float has higher precision)",
